tests/vendor — third-party files used by tests only (A-16 "Real r128 in tests", CTO F3 review H2)

three-r128.min.js
  What:    three.js r128 global build, package three@0.128.0, file package/build/three.min.js (MIT, licence header kept).
  Why:     cdnjs.cloudflare.com is blocked in the build workspace; registry.npmjs.org is reachable. Tests fulfil ONLY the
           exact cdnjs URL of the brief (https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js) with this
           file through page.route (tests/helpers/browser.mjs, three: 'real'). The app, src/index.html, dist/index.html
           and build.mjs never reference this folder; the published page keeps loading r128 from cdnjs.
           tests/lint-constraints.mjs fails if the build output ever contains the three.js licence banner.
  Tarball: https://registry.npmjs.org/three/-/three-0.128.0.tgz (6 543 441 bytes)
           integrity sha512-i0ap/E+OaSfzw7bD1TtYnPo3VEplkl70WX5fZqZnfZsE3k3aSFudqrrC9ldFZfYFkn1zwDmBcdGfiIm/hnbyZA==
           (= `npm view three@0.128.0 dist.integrity`)
  File:    603 445 bytes, sha512sum
           74bc547a50299d8c692ede8ada2a261a78271cef37894bd9cad0376230d40a34f41c33872979d561d7f7854e098ccf2e121c5ff670f5fdecbdf14deddaf674a9
  Refetch (in an empty scratch directory):
           npm pack three@0.128.0            # or: curl -sO https://registry.npmjs.org/three/-/three-0.128.0.tgz
           openssl dgst -sha512 -binary three-0.128.0.tgz | base64 -w0    # must equal the integrity above
           tar -xzf three-0.128.0.tgz package/build/three.min.js
           cp package/build/three.min.js <repo>/tests/vendor/three-r128.min.js
           sha512sum <repo>/tests/vendor/three-r128.min.js                 # must equal the file hash above
  Note:    byte identity with the cdnjs copy cannot be checked from here; it is the same r128 release and
           tests/e2e/view3d-real.spec.mjs asserts THREE.REVISION === '128'.

three-0.180.0/three.webgpu.min.js, three-0.180.0/three.core.min.js   (G1, QA_GPU only)
  What:    three.js 0.180.0 WebGPU build (package three@0.180.0, files package/build/three.webgpu.min.js and
           package/build/three.core.min.js, MIT, licence headers kept). three.webgpu.min.js imports ./three.core.min.js.
  Why:     the /gpu page (dist/gpu/index.html) imports
           https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/0.180.0/three.webgpu.min.js from its bootstrap script (CD-10).
           tests/helpers/gpu.mjs fulfils that URL (and the ./three.core.min.js next to it) with these files through
           page.route; the app, src/ and dist/ never reference this folder (lint: one external URL on /gpu, and the
           0.180 licence banner must never be inlined).
